    <bpmn:process id="W_W1970" name="W1970. Institutional Account Billing &amp; Collection" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Institutional account purchase; monthly billing cycle
Frequency: Monthly billing; ~50–100 active institutional accounts
Volume: ~100–200 institutional invoices/year
Owner: AR Clerk
Participants: AR Clerk, Trade Account Manager, Credit Analyst
Source: workflow W1970 — Institutional Account Billing &amp; Collection</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1970_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1970_Lane1" name="AR Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1970_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1970_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1970_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1970_Lane2" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1970_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1970_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1970_Start4" name="Institutional account purchase; monthly billing cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1970_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1970_Task5" name="AR Clerk processes institutional account billing: (a) standard trade billing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AR Clerk processes institutional account billing: (a) standard trade billing per W8, (b) institutional accounts: schools, hospitals, churches, NGOs — processed like trade accounts with standard BIR invoice, (c) VAT: standard 12% (no special government VAT treatment), (d) EWT: may apply depending on institutional type (private entities may or may not withhold)
Responsible (R): AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Accounting Manager
Duration: Per billing cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1970_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1970_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1970_Task6" name="Collection: (a) standard collection process per W108, (b) institutional…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Collection: (a) standard collection process per W108, (b) institutional accounts: typically better payers than government but may have budget cycle constraints (schools: aligned to school year; churches: aligned to liturgical calendar; NGOs: aligned to donor funding cycles), (c) terms: Net 30 standard; Net 60 for established accounts
Responsible (R): AR Clerk / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Accounting Manager
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1970_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1970_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1970_Task7" name="Overdue management: (a) standard escalation per W108, (b) for institutional…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Overdue management: (a) standard escalation per W108, (b) for institutional accounts: Trade Account Manager contacts account directly, (c) payment plan offered for legitimate financial difficulty (common with smaller NGOs and schools)
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: Per overdue</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1970_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1970_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1970_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1970_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-381 (ensure controlled execution — Government Billing, Collection &amp; Compliance (PA-46.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: AR Clerk</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
